# Pomni's workspace — all of it, runtime and records alike.
#
# It used to be half-tracked: the runtime under here was ignored and the records — projects,
# backlog, repo entries, workflows — were committed, so that state travelled with the code and
# could be read in a diff. That split cost more than it paid. It let `git checkout` rewind the
# item counter and reissue live ids (POMN-57), it made `repo sync` dirty a tracked file and
# refuse the next checkout (POMN-52), and it meant a run's `git add -A` swept Pomni's own state
# into commits of code. Untracking the whole directory closes all three at once.
#
# What it costs, stated plainly: a fresh clone has no backlog. These records live on the machine
# that holds them, and nowhere else, unless you put them somewhere yourself.
.pomni/

# local env
.env
.env.local

# Scratch an agent leaves behind. It has happened; a `git add -A` then commits it.
/_*.mjs
/_*.js
/*.tmp
